    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Orgs where the count of active SBQQ__PriceRule__c exceeds a healthy threshold (typically 50+).
Why it matters: Each price rule adds calculation time. Above the threshold, configurator load and quote-line recalc slow noticeably; large quotes risk governor limits.
Suppress a finding: when the high count is genuine business complexity and performance has been benchmarked acceptable.
Disable the detector: only if you&apos;ve engineered around the cost. Most should leave this on as a performance early warning.</value></values>
